1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Bid teams often lose before writing begins.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,000
They chase weak fits, then ignore the buyer's score.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,500
BidPilot starts with eligibility, capacity, and comparable delivery.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:20,000
This run is PURSUE. Other inputs produce REVIEW and NO-GO.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The official evaluation matrix becomes the control plane.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The 40-point criterion leads, with supplier assets and an owner.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,500
The agent compares three materially different Win Positions.

8
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:50,000
The selected position follows the buyer's highest-weighted need.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,500
Eight fragments form four score-bearing proposal responses.

10
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:05,000
The editable draft passes review and downloads from the Bid Room.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Red-team gaps become twelve owned and governed tasks.

12
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:20,500
Snowpark decides. Cortex Code writes. Snowflake preserves the run.

13
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:26,000
This is a replayable operating workflow, not a prompt wrapper.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Should we bid, and how do we win the score.
